WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Welcome to the Everyday Hero Academy first aid course.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.160
Today, we're going to cover a wide range of first aid skills that you can use in

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.240
all sorts of situations, from minor scrapes in a non-emergency,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.600
to life-saving actions during a major crisis.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.680
As we go through these modules, I want you to keep one thing in mind.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.559
Communication is key. If you are acting as a caregiver and an incident happens,

00:00:24.559 --> 00:00:28.799
your priority is to reach out to the parent or guardian immediately.

00:00:28.799 --> 00:00:32.480
To make that easier, it's a great idea to always keep a file with their

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.599
emergency contact info right where you can find it.

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:39.759
It is also best practice to document these conversations by keeping a simple

00:00:39.759 --> 00:00:42.799
record of what happened and when you spoke to the family.

00:00:42.799 --> 00:00:46.480
Most importantly, if you are facing a true medical emergency,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.480
remember the order of operations. Call 911 first,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:55.520
and then call the parents as soon as it is safe to do so.

